---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Banner from '../components/Banner.astro';
import FeatureCard from '../components/FeatureCard.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Behind the Corner" description="A place to explore and learn about various topics that spark curiosity.">
  
  <section>
    <p>Welcome to Curiosity Corner, a Windhoek based space driven entirely by creative experiments, manual labor, and questionable corporate management. To understand how this shop works, you first need to meet the team.</p>
    
    <h4>The CEO & Creative Director: Dexter</h4>

    <p>
      <span class="image left"><img src="../../../../public/about/dexter.jpeg" style="width: 150px; height: auto;"></span>
      <strong>Age: </strong> 2 years <br/>
      <strong>Breed: </strong> Ginger Cat (possesses exactly one shared brain cell)<br/>
      <strong>Qualifications: </strong> Can stare at a blank wall for four hours; has zero respect for boundaries; highly motivated by wet food.
    </p>

    <p>Dexter is the undisputed mastermind behind this operation. He doesn't have opposable thumbs, but what he lacks in physical dexterity, he makes up for in pure, tyrannical micromanagement. He holds 100% of the equity and 0% of the responsibility. If a product appears in the shop, it is because Dexter stared at it, knocked it off a table, or slept on the packaging until I agreed to make it.</p>

    <h3>Chief of Opposable Thumbs & SQL Queries: Yolinda</h3>
    <p><strong>Age: </strong> Mind your business<br/>
      <strong>Qualifications: </strong> 15+ years as a Developer, Project Manager, Business Owner, and Data Analyst. <br/> 
      <strong>Core Duties: </strong> Doing all the actual crafting, packing, and shipping because the Boss refuses to work weekends.</p>


    <p>I am a natural introvert, but I have a relentless, optimistic energy when it comes to learning how things are made. For over fifteen years, my day job has involved staring at glowing screens, writing complex SQL queries, and analyzing mountains of data in Windhoek. But let’s be honest - ’n mens se brein kan net soveel data hanteer voor jy heeltemal mal word. Eventually, I just needed to step away from the keyboard and make something physical that I could actually hold in my hands.</p>

    <p>So I started experimenting with different crafts, and I quickly discovered that I have a very short attention span. I can’t just learn one thing and stick to it. I need to explore, experiment, and try new things constantly. This is why you’ll find a wide variety of products in this shop - from hand-sewn bags to hand-knitted scarves, from hand-carved wooden spoons to hand-painted ceramics. If it’s made by hand, it’s probably something I’ve tried my hand at.</p>

    <p>But my curious nature also means I’ve learned what I absolutely despise. I once tried to learn how to sew and knit, and nee dankie—those hobbies were swiftly banished to the "never again" pile.</p>

    <h3>The Corporate Philosophy: No Niches, Just Fixations</h3>
    <p>Because I strongly prefer to stay happily behind the scenes and off-camera, this brand isn't about my face - it's entirely about the craft and Dexter's erratic leadership.</p>

    <p>We don't do rigid corporate categories, boring product niches, or five-year inventory plans. If I try a new creative skill, fall in love with the process, and make something high-quality, I will put it up here for you to buy. If Dexter’s curiosity (or my own hyper-fixation) leads us to a completely different medium next month? Well, dan speel ons met iets nuuts.</p>

    <p>Whether you're here to buy something unique we’ve made, grab a hassle-free kit, or just see what crazy DIY project we're tackling next, we’re glad you stopped by.</p>

    <p>Welkom by die hoekie.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>